{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1459284-deviant-some-questions","id":1459284,"title":"[Deviant] Some Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-08T05:38:36-07:00","id":1459284,"title":"[Deviant] Some Questions","content":"I got a little confused by a few things.<br /> Variations, Scars and Deviations are quite complicated and hard to keep the exact rules for them in my head straight while paging back and forth during character creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Increase the Deviation Magnitude by one if one or more entangled Variations are likely to create story complications by being \u201calways-on,\u201d such as Camouflage 3+, Gigantic, Miniaturization, or Out of Phase (Body) 3. </div> </div> </div>Ok, so wait. If I pick one of those and attach Relentless to it, does that mean that the Variation costs more? Or does the Scar cost less? Or... More? Or... Is it both Variation and Scar costing more? Ummmmmmmmmmmmmm....<br /> <br /> Also, the different types and what Variation can go with what Scar is a little confusing. I often have to wonder if I made an invalid combination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T05:47:20-07:00","id":1459286,"title":"","content":"Deviations increase the Magnitude of the trait they're attached to. A Deviation on a Variation modifies the Variation's Magnitude by the indicated amount. A Deviation on a Scar modifies the Scar Magnitude by the indicated amount.<br /> <br /> Relentless Variation is a Deviation that applies to a Scar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T06:58:50-07:00","id":1459296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1459284-deviant-some-questions#post1459284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the different types and what Variation can go with what Scar is a little confusing. I often have to wonder if I made an invalid combination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the Variation says otherwise (like Rapid Healing and those three specific aspects of Anomalous Biology), any type of Variation can go with any type of Scar. The type of Scar is what determines how/if the Variation is activated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T12:10:36-07:00","id":1459325,"title":"","content":"Let's use concrete examples.<br /> <br /> Say you take Boneless \u25cf\u25cf, which makes your body pliable like that of an octopus. Two-dot Variation, must be entangled with at least a two-dot Scar. You take Deterioration \u25cf\u25cf, a Controlled Scar. Since it's a Controlled Scar, the action to turn Boneless on for a scene requires a Scar Finesse roll. The specific effects of Deterioration add a Scar Resistance roll when you successfully activate Boneless. If you fail the Resistance roll, you suffer a debilitating Tilt.<br /> <br /> Now let's say you add the Defensive Deviation to Boneless. This makes the activation of Boneless reflexive, so it doesn't take a turn and you can do it as an immediate response, like if squishing through somewhere will get you out of range of an attack. It's a (+1 Magnitude) Deviation, meaning Boneless's effective Magnitude raises to \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, even though you don't get the benefits of Boneless \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf (so you're not full-on liquid, just a squishy octopus mass still). It's like a phantom dot of Magnitude, or you could think of it as Variation 2 + Deviation 1 = Total Magnitude 3.<br /> <br /> Defensive Boneless now counts as a three-dot Variation though, which means it must be entangled with at least a three-dot Scar, meaning Deterioration \u25cf\u25cf is not enough. To match this, you could simply raise the Scar's Magnitude by a dot to Deterioration \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, which makes you choose either the Lingering, Painful, or Severe effect listed for that Scar. Say you take Painful. Now activating Boneless is reflexive, but since it's still entangled to Deterioration, which is a Controlled Scar, you still need to make the Scar Finesse roll, and on success you not only still need to roll Scar Resistance, but Painful Deterioration also inflicts a point of bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Let's say you don't want to take Lingering, Painful, or Severe, though. You could instead increase Deterioration's total Magnitude with a Scar Deviation. Deterioration has no listed Deviations of its own, but page 170 has a list of Standard Scar Deviations that aren't specific to individual Scars. You take one dot of Identifier. Deterioration \u25cf\u25cf + Identifier \u25cf counts as a Magnitude \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Scar to entangle with Defensive Boneless. In this configuration you can activate Boneless reflexively. You need to make both the Scar Finesse roll and the Scar Resistance roll, but instead of taking bashing damage, you ooze some kind of octo-oil residue that can be used to track you down easier.<br /> <br /> What happens if you take a different kind of Scar? Let's stay on Defensive Boneless but replace Deterioration altogether. This time we'll take Silence \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, a Persistent Scar, meaning something about octopus mode makes our vocal cords stop working. Here's a benefit of entangling Variations with Persistent Scars: you don't have to roll to activate them! Boneless has the Toggled keyword, which means you're not stuck as an octopus mass forever. You still turn Boneless on or off, and if you didn't have Defensive you'd still have to take a turn to do it. Defensive means you don't even need to spend a turn doing it and can just freely turn your bones on and off.<br /> <br /> Deviations let Variations and Scars do different things off the beaten path of their core progression. Variation Deviations make the power better but require bigger Scars. Scar Deviations make the Scar worse but allow bigger Variations. Some Deviations are <i>negative,</i> like (-1 Magnitude), in which case you reverse this. So negative Scar Deviations make the Scar less bad, but don't allow Variations as big.<br /> <br /> Invalid combinations fall into two major categories. One is Standard Scar Deviations that specify what type of Scar they can modify. Suppressible Variation, for example, allows you to temporarily shut off a Variation that's otherwise always on, and therefore the entangled Scar has to be Persistent so that it <i>is</i> always on in the first place. The other is the Only keywords. Target Restriction, for example, is Directed-Only. It's a Scar Deviation that only lets you aim at certain kinds of targets, so it has to be entangled with Directed Variations that aim at particular targets in the first place.<br /> <br /> When entangling Scars, check for the Only Keywords. If you're looking at the list of Scar Deviations that aren't specific to individual Scars, check the Scar Type. If you don't have a conflicting Only Keyword or a mismatched Scar Type, you're golden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T10:30:01-07:00","id":1461049,"title":"","content":"Forgive me if I am overstepping but as there is no deviant forum yet I thought I would post my own deviant question here as well. Could someone please offer me example of what they mean by a &quot;secondary Variation&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T10:48:46-07:00","id":1461056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darklander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1459284-deviant-some-questions?p=1461049#post1461049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if I am overstepping but as there is no deviant forum yet I thought I would post my own deviant question here as well. Could someone please offer me example of what they mean by a &amp;quot;secondary Variation&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Variation that exists as part of another Variation like Sacred Flesh or Monstrous Transformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T22:36:59-07:00","id":1461155,"title":"","content":"Some Variations or Scars nest others of the same type within. For example, Monstrous Transformation gives you one toggled supernatural form you shift into. You pick a set of secondary Variations whose Magnitude can be supported collectively by the entangled Scar, and instead of using those Variation powers normally, you get all of them activated at once, but only while transformed. You don't actually &quot;have&quot; those secondary Variations in terms of sheet math. You &quot;have&quot; Monstrous Transformation, and the effect of your Monstrous Transformation is the same as if you did have those other Variations while transformed.<br /> <br /> Secondary Scars are more common than secondary Variations, since you can entangle multiple Variations to one Scar already, but not vice-versa, so they're more important to customizing Scars. Persistent Drawback is the easy example to point to. The effect of the Persistent Drawback Scar is that it's a Controlled Scar that makes you pick a secondary Persistent Scar of equal effective Magnitude, and while your entangled Variations are active, you suffer the effects of that secondary Scar. Once again, you don't &quot;have&quot; two Scars here, you have one sheet-wise, but its effect is to borrow the mechanics from the other Scar. (If you're wondering why anyone would ever take a Persistent Scar directly and suffer the penalty all the time instead of folding it through Persistent Drawback and suffering the penalty only while using the power, the Scar you &quot;actually have&quot; is Persistent Drawback, which is Controlled. Controlled entanglements require Scar Finesse rolls to activate those powers, while Persistent entanglements don't.)<br /> <br /> We may not have a Deviant subforum, but I wonder if we would have enough attention to merit an &quot;Ask a simple question, get a simple answer - Deviant: the Renegades&quot; thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 09-24-2021, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T21:36:57-07:00","id":1462072,"title":"","content":"Thanks for enlightening me on secondary variations, but I have another question. Could the Cheiron Group from Hunter: The Vigil theoretically be used as a Deviant conspiracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T21:56:04-07:00","id":1462074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darklander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1459284-deviant-some-questions?p=1462072#post1462072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for enlightening me on secondary variations, but I have another question. Could the Cheiron Group from Hunter: The Vigil theoretically be used as a Deviant conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a rule, core books generally don't make direct references to other game lines. That being said, the Conspiracies in 2E Hunter have a lot of similarities with the conspiracies in Deviant, and Cheiron is definitely the closest to a crossover point between the game lines, thematically speaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}